idn't bind. It still resolved default for factor values. Could use legacy flattened keys. The skill says legacy only for deliberately flattened keys. But maybe MCP's \\\"21.01\\\" still expects flattened keys? Need inspect previous run_trace tool run payload? The MCP request.json may contain our payload. Let's look at evidence files for run 008.\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough\":{\"turn_id\":\"01a00c20-7ae9-7612-ad47-9985844e3b9d\"}}}\n/codex_home/sessions/2026/08/16/rollout-2026-08-16T19-50-49-01a00c20-792b-7453-8b04-99af26a0fc37.jsonl:300:{\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-16T19:59:37.209Z\",\"type\":\"response_item\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"function_call_output\",\"id\":\"fco_01a00c28-84f7-7052-be73-86b2f9483bde\",\"call_id\":\"call_00_wY2bNe7ukUTDhHnj0mzR6000\",\"output\":\"Chunk ID: c20ae1\\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\\nProcess exited with code 0\\nOriginal token count: 5353\\nOutput:\\n--- /workspace/run_trace/galaxy_tool_run_008/request.json\\n{\\n  \\\"history_id\\\": \\\"bbd44e69cb8906b5179685b1c44a0eff\\\",\\n  \\\"input_format\\\": \\\"21.01\\\",\\n  \\\"selected_input_format\\\": \\\"21.01\\\",\\n  \\\"tool_id\\\": \\\"toolshed.g2.bx.psu.edu/repos/iuc/deseq2/deseq2/2.11.40.8+galaxy4\\\",\\n  \\\"tool_inputs\\\": {\\n    \\\"advanced_options\\\": {\\n      \\\"auto_mean_filter_off\\\": false,\\n      \\\"esf_cond\\\": {\\n        \\\"esf\\\": \\\"\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"fit_type\\\": \\\"1\\\",\\n      \\\"lfc_shrinkage_type\\\": \\\"normal\\\",\\n      \\\"outlier_filter_off\\\": false,\\n      \\\"outlier_replace_off\\\": false,\\n      \\\"prefilter_conditional\\\": {\\n        \\\"prefilter\\\": \\\"\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"use_beta_priors\\\": false\\n    },\\n    \\\"header\\\": true,\\n    \\\"output_options\\\": {\\n      \\\"alpha_ma\\\": 0.1,\\n      \\\"output_selector\\\": []\\n    },\\n    \\\"select_data\\\": {\\n      \\\"how\\\": \\\"datasets_per_level\\\",\\n      \\\"rep_factorName\\\": [\\n       